            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0404" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Colonel J. Hart Caughey to the Committee
                        of Three</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-02">2 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following is Trusum No. 17, dated 31 January 1946:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote"><p>“The Chihfeng, Jehol, situation has now clarified and it
                        is confirmed by the field team there that the pacification troops
                        (Communist) have entirely withdrawn from all areas which they occupied after
                        2400 hours 13 January. They had taken over certain villages east of the town
                        upon this withdrawal of the Russian garrison on 23 January, but they had
                        been in Chihfeng and vicinity ever since August 1945. The strength of the
                        pacification corps in Chihfeng city is now reported as 800 (a field team was
                        dispatched from Peiping to Chengte, Jehol Province, on 31 January).
                    [”]</p></quote>
                <p>[Here follows report of activities of certain other truce teams.]</p>
                <closer><signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hart Caughey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
